      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-amendment-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-amendment-act-2005.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914\n\n15XMA  Requesting State agencies or Territory agencies to issue\nevidence of assumed identities etc.\n(1) An issuing agency that is a State agency of a particular State and\nthat receives a request under section 15XL must comply with the\nrequest to the extent that the laws of the State require it to do so.\n(2) An issuing agency that is a Territory agency of a particular\nTerritory and that receives a request under section 15XL must\ncomply with the request to the extent that the laws of the Territory\nrequire it to do so.\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 26 May 2005\nSenate on 14 June 2005]\n(73/05)",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914\n\n15XMA  Requesting State agencies or Territory agencies to issue\nevidence of assumed identities etc.\n(1) An issuing agency that is a State agency of a particular State and\nthat receives a request under section 15XL must comply with the\nrequest to the extent that the laws of the State require it to do so.\n(2) An issuing agency that is a Territory agency of a particular\nTerritory and that receives a request under section 15XL must\ncomply with the request to the extent that the laws of the Territory\nrequire it to do so.\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 26 May 2005\nSenate on 14 June 2005]\n(73/05)",
